  "phrases": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Beer almost always comes in brown glass, because light physically breaks beer.",
      "start": 0.071,
      "end": 3.657,
      "wordRange": [
        0,
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hops",
      "text": "Hops leave compounds in the liquid that are stable in the dark.",
      "start": 3.949,
      "end": 6.754,
      "wordRange": [
        12,
        23
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "riboflavin",
      "text": "Hit them with blue and ultraviolet light, and riboflavin, a vitamin already in the beer, acts as a middleman.",
      "start": 7.038,
      "end": 12.468,
      "wordRange": [
        24,
        42
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "shatter",
      "text": "It absorbs the light and hands the energy along until those hop compounds shatter into something chemically close to skunk spray. That is not a figure of speech.",
      "start": 12.748,
      "end": 20.284,
      "wordRange": [
        43,
        70
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "glass",
      "text": "Brown glass blocks nearly all of those wavelengths. Green blocks a fraction, which is why some imports taste faintly like a warning.",
      "start": 20.593,
      "end": 26.708,
      "wordRange": [
        71,
        92
      ]
    }
  ],
